nodecode-health-insights is a rewrite of mwdearing's mwdearing/hermes-health-insights:

  https://github.com/mwdearing/hermes-health-insights
  commit d6d09c1f17ada6ca60368a1e0c7a7b5bd4efefc6
  Apache-2.0, Copyright (c) mwdearing (the repository's LICENSE keeps its
  holder line as the template's "[yyyy] [name of copyright owner]"; the
  author is mwdearing in plugin.json) (LICENSE)

What was rewritten: the original's deterministic analysis, in Lisp. The
weekly report (a 7-day mean against a 28-day median, and a direction only
past one MAD-based sigma), the concern rules for blood pressure, resting
heart rate, HRV, sleep, oxygen saturation and data gaps, and the coverage and
freshness report all read the same receiver database: samples, sleep_sessions
and sync_runs, with SELECT only. The task's shape changed with the harness:
the original is ten skills driving a Python command line tool, and this is one
cell whose own tool and /vitals command answer the same questions.

What was left out: the modules the original ships beyond its core (GLP-1
monitoring, medication adherence through an external medlog command line,
nutrition against the DRI tables, the labs database, workouts and ECG), the
YAML configuration of units and profile, the optional narration model, and
the synthetic demo database. The time zone comes from the section's
utc_offset_hours rather than a named zone, because the image carries no
time-zone database. The advice wording is the original's, shortened.
